### Page 1 of 2

```text
FINANCE COMMITTEE
MINUTES
A meeting of the Finance Committee was held on Monday, October21, 2024, in Committee Room
104 and via electronic meeting, starting at 12:00 p.m. Those in attendance were as follows:
COMMITTEE MEMBERS:
Jeff’ White, Acting Chairman; Dr. Michelle Aldrich (via Zoom).
Chairwoman; Bryan Cook; and Richard Johnson (via Zoom).
AGENDA ITEMS
8.
ORDINANCE —2 READING -Authorizing the Contractor Licensing Board to license
and otherwise regulate portable fire extinguisher, hose station equipment and hood system
cleaning and maintenance professionals, making confonning amendments, and repealing
obsolete provisions of the
Municipal
Code of the City of Cheyenne,
Wyoming.
(SPONSOR
- DR. ALDRICH)
Mr. Cook moved to approve on 2 reading, seconded by Dr. Aldrich. Motion carried with Dr.
Aldrich and Mr. Cook voting “YES” and Mr. Johnson voting “NO.”
Battalion Chief Bob Mason, Fire & Rescue Department, provided a staff report and Kris Jones,
City Clerk, provided additional information. Chairman White and committee members Aldrich,
Cook, and Johnson commented on the item.
18.
LEASES/CONTRACTS/LEGAL:
d)
Agreement between the City of Cheyenne, Transit Division, and the Wyoming
Department of Health, Aging Division to provide transportation support services to
persons 60 years or older under the Title 111-B Program Grant for FY 2025. (Title
Ill-B Division of Aging Grant)
Mr. Cook moved to approve in an amount not to exceed 562,620.00, seconded by Dr. Aldrich.
Motion carried by unanimous voice vote.
Vicki Nemecek. Public Works Director, provided a staff report and advised the agreement is
revenue to the city.
20.
CONSIDERATION OF BIDS/PURCHASES/REQUESTS FOR PROPOSALS:
e)
Consideration of Bid #S-6-25 for an Agreement between the City of Cheyenne and
Pine Bluffs Gravel & Excavating, Inc. for the Childs Draw South Tributary
Drainage Enhancements Project. (General Fund, General Fund Reserves)
```

### Page 2 of 2

```text
Mr. Cook moved to accept the bid in an amount not to exceed $465,104.75, seconded by Dr.
Aldrich. Motion carried by unanimous voice vote.
Tom Cobb, City Engineer, provided a staff report and TJ Barttelbort, Purchasing Manager,
provided additional information. Chairman White and committee members Cook and Johnson
commented on the item.
There being no thither items for the agenda to come before the Finance Committee, the meeting
was adjourned at 12:17 p.m.
